System Requirements Specification (SRS)
Employee Attendance Management System
1. Introduction
1.1 Project Overview
The Employee Attendance Management System is a comprehensive web-based application designed to digitize and streamline attendance tracking, leave management, and daily reporting for organizations. The system replaces manual attendance registers with an automated, efficient, and user-friendly platform that reduces paperwork, minimizes errors, and provides real-time insights into workforce activity.

1.2 Project Purpose
The primary purpose of developing this system is to:

Automate Attendance Tracking: Digitize the traditional way of marking attendance with check-in/out functionality 

Centralize Leave Management: Streamline leave requests, approvals, and balance tracking

Generate Custom Reports: Provide detailed attendance and performance reports for administrative decision-making

Enhance Security: Enforce office IP-based attendance validation and role-based access control

Improve User Experience: Offer responsive design for both desktop and mobile access

1.3 Scope
The system covers:

Employee check-in/out with office IP validation

Leave requests (Paid, Carried, Unpaid, Emergency, Sick, Privilege)

Daily report submission with department-specific templates

Admin/SuperAdmin dashboards with workforce analytics

User management and role-based access control

Holiday management and calendar views

Device request management for employee devices

Activity logging and audit trails

2. Stakeholders 
2.1 Primary Stakeholders
Stakeholder	Role
Employees	End-users who check-in/out, apply for leave, and submit daily reports
Managers/Admins	Monitor attendance, approve leaves, manage users
SuperAdmins	Full system control including user deletion and role changes
2.2 Secondary Stakeholders
Stakeholder	Role
HR Department	Manages employee records, leave policies
IT Department	Manages office IPs, device approvals, system maintenance
Management	Views reports for workforce planning
3. User Requirements 
ID	Requirement	Description
UR-01	User Authentication	Secure login with mobile number and password
UR-02	Role-Based Dashboards	Customized dashboards for Employee, Admin, SuperAdmin
UR-03	Check-in/Check-out	Mark attendance with office IP validation
UR-04	Leave Requests	Apply for leave with category selection (Paid, Carried, Unpaid, Emergency, Sick, Privilege)
UR-05	Daily Reports	Submit daily work reports with quantity and duration
UR-06	View Attendance	View personal attendance history in table or calendar view
UR-07	Request Corrections	Request corrections for incorrect attendance records
UR-08	View Team Reports	Admins view all employee reports
UR-09	Manage Users	Admins add, update, and view employees
UR-10	Manage Holidays	Admins add/view holidays
UR-11	Office IP Management	Admins manage approved IP addresses for attendance
UR-12	Device Requests	Employees request device approval; Admins approve/reject
UR-13	Activity Logs	Admins view system activity logs
UR-14	Notifications	Email notifications for leave requests
UR-15	Responsive Design	Accessible on both desktop and mobile devices
4. System Requirements 
ID	Requirement	Description
SR-01	Performance	Handle multiple concurrent users with minimal latency
SR-02	Security	JWT-based authentication; bcrypt password hashing
SR-03	Data Integrity	SQLAlchemy ORM with MySQL database
SR-04	Scalability	Modular architecture supporting future growth
SR-05	Reliability	99.9% uptime target with error logging
SR-06	Compatibility	Support Chrome, Firefox, Edge, Safari browsers
SR-07	Maintainability	Clean, documented code with separation of concerns
SR-08	Accessibility	WCAG-compliant UI with keyboard navigation
SR-09	Data Backup	Automated database backups
SR-10	Audit Trail	Complete activity logging for compliance
5. Functional Requirements
5.1 Authentication Module
ID	Function	Description
FR-AUTH-01	Login	Employee/Admin login with mobile + password
FR-AUTH-02	JWT Session	Token-based session management
FR-AUTH-03	Password Reset	Forgot password with email reset link
FR-AUTH-04	Device Tracking	Track device fingerprint for security
5.2 Attendance Module
ID	Function	Description
FR-ATT-01	Check-in	Employee check-in with office IP validation
FR-ATT-02	Check-out	Employee check-out with office IP validation
FR-ATT-03	Office IP Validation	Restrict attendance to approved office IPs
FR-ATT-04	Late Check-in Reason	Require reason for check-in after 10:30 AM
FR-ATT-05	Early Check-out Reason	Require reason for check-out before 6:30 PM
FR-ATT-06	Report Validation	Require daily report before check-out
FR-ATT-07	Attendance History	View attendance history (table/calendar)
FR-ATT-08	Attendance Summary	Monthly summary with Present, Half Day, Absent, Holiday, Leave counts
FR-ATT-09	Half Day Requests	Employees request half-day (morning/afternoon slots)
FR-ATT-10	Attendance Corrections	Employees request corrections; Admins approve/reject
