8. Database Schema
The system contains 19 tables:

#	Table	Description
1	users	All system users
2	attendance	Daily attendance records
3	attendance_corrections	Attendance correction requests
4	leave_types	Leave type definitions
5	leave_requests	Leave applications
6	notification_emails	Email recipients for notifications
7	leave_notification_emails	Junction table for leave-email notifications
8	holidays	Company holiday list
9	device_requests	Device registration requests
10	office_ips	Approved office IP addresses
11	half_day_requests	Half day requests
12	leave_encashment_requests	Leave encashment requests
13	password_reset_tokens	Password reset tokens
14	activity_logs	User activity audit logs
15	company_settings	Company configuration
16	report_departments	Report departments (B2B/B2C/HR/IT)
17	report_types	Report types per department
18	report_subtypes	Report subtypes per type
19	daily_reports	Employee daily reports
9. Use Cases (Key Scenarios)
9.1 Employee Check-in
Employee logs in to the system

Employee navigates to Dashboard

Employee clicks "Check In"

System validates IP address against office_ips table

If IP is approved, system records check-in with timestamp

If IP is not approved, system shows error message

9.2 Employee Check-out with Report Validation
Employee logs in and submits daily report

Employee clicks "Check Out"

System validates IP address and report submission status

If both pass, system records check-out timestamp

System calculates and updates attendance status

9.3 Leave Application
Employee navigates to Leave page

Employee selects leave category, dates, and reason

System validates leave balance (for Paid/Carried leaves)

Admin approves/rejects request

System updates leave balance on approval

9.4 Admin Report Viewing
Admin navigates to Admin Reports page

Admin selects employee from dropdown

Admin selects month/year

System displays reports for selected employee

